[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4584733116","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119902#issuecomment-4584733116","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119902","id":4584733116,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABEUV5vA","user":{"login":"van800","id":1482681,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0ODI2ODE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1482681?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800","html_url":"https://github.com/van800","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-30T20:53:58Z","updated_at":"2026-05-30T20:53:58Z","body":"cc: @Temptica","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4584733116/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4667242596","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119902#issuecomment-4667242596","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119902","id":4667242596,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABFjB4ZA","user":{"login":"van800","id":1482681,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0ODI2ODE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1482681?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800","html_url":"https://github.com/van800","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-10T06:33:19Z","updated_at":"2026-06-10T06:33:19Z","body":"The PR doesn't brake the ability to have different editors for GDScript and C#. However, if there is already Rider for GDScript and the Rider for C# is missing, this PR updates it. And this logic makes sense to me.\r\nI have a bigger proposal to unify external editors for all possible file formats https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/14924, which would also cover the case in this PR.\r\n\r\nI am the author of both PathLocator and Rider addon.\r\n\r\nPathLocator is a fast sync call.\r\nhttps://github.com/JetBrains/resharper-unity/tree/master/unity/PathLocator\r\n\r\nRider addon is async, can be slow.\r\nhttps://github.com/JetBrains/godot-support/tree/master/godot-editor-addon/native/rider-plugin/src\r\nOn Linux it calls `locate` utility, which I don't call in the PathLocator. \r\n\r\nTechnically I can add async logic in the `PathLocator`, release a new version on nuget, rewrite the logic on the Godot side to run the new async logic on backgroud and update the setting when ready. But for the Godot C# the workflow is not suitable for that. In Godot C# when external editor is not Rider we don't do Rider path finding in advance. When user switches the external editor to be Rider, we need to find Rider immediately, it would be weird UX to show a modal progress of searching for path.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4667242596/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4668911125","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119902#issuecomment-4668911125","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119902","id":4668911125,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABFknuFQ","user":{"login":"raulsntos","id":3903059,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5MDMwNTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3903059?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos","html_url":"https://github.com/raulsntos","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-10T10:02:21Z","updated_at":"2026-06-10T10:02:21Z","body":"> The PR doesn't brake the ability to have different editors for GDScript and C#. However, if there is already Rider for GDScript and the Rider for C# is missing, this PR updates it. And this logic makes sense to me.\r\n\r\nWhat I meant is that these are different settings owned by different areas, so it feels weird to mix them. If the user doesn't want to override the general editor, they could set the C# setting to \"Disabled\". Wouldn't that also fix the issue?\r\n\r\n> When user switches the external editor to be Rider, we need to find Rider immediately, it would be weird UX to show a modal progress of searching for path.\r\n\r\nI don't think we need to find Rider immediately. The `InitializeIfNeeded` method is called when the setting changes, and there's some time between that and the time the user tries to open a file, I would hope the async lookup is fast enough to be complete before that.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nPersonally, I don't mind making this change but it doesn't seem to be very useful, because it relies on the general editor settings being configured for Rider. So it doesn't really fix the issue. If we have to take a different approach to fix the issue for users that don't have Rider configured for GDScript, then that would also apply to this scenario.\r\n\r\nThat said, this seems like a reasonable stopgap for now, if we don't want to wait until implementing the more complicated solution.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4668911125/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4669879063","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119902#issuecomment-4669879063","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119902","id":4669879063,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABFlizFw","user":{"login":"van800","id":1482681,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0ODI2ODE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1482681?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800","html_url":"https://github.com/van800","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-10T11:54:02Z","updated_at":"2026-06-10T11:54:02Z","body":"> set the C# setting to \"Disabled\". Wouldn't that also fix the issue?\r\n\r\nThis causes opening C# files in the internal editor.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4669879063/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4669900452","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119902#issuecomment-4669900452","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119902","id":4669900452,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABFlkGpA","user":{"login":"van800","id":1482681,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0ODI2ODE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1482681?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800","html_url":"https://github.com/van800","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-10T11:56:29Z","updated_at":"2026-06-10T11:56:29Z","body":"I see adoption of the Rider addon among users in the csharp channels in the Godot/GodotCafe discords, so it feels it would be useful change.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4669900452/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4670885661","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119902#issuecomment-4670885661","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119902","id":4670885661,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABFmgPHQ","user":{"login":"van800","id":1482681,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0ODI2ODE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1482681?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800","html_url":"https://github.com/van800","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/use